  {
   "sentence": 1,
   "text": "In 1925, a con man sold the Eiffel Tower. It was never his to sell.",
   "first_word": "In",
   "asr_first": "In",
   "word_start": 0.4,
   "onset": 0.4,
   "speech_end": 5.28,
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.59
  },
  {
   "sentence": 2,
   "text": "His name was Victor Lustig. A newspaper story about the tower's upkeep gave him an idea.",
   "first_word": "His",
   "asr_first": "His",
   "word_start": 5.65,
   "onset": 5.65,
   "speech_end": 10.4,
   "start": 5.59,
   "end": 10.75,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 3,
   "text": "He posed as a government official. He forged official stationery. Then he invited scrap metal dealers to a luxury hotel in Paris.",
   "first_word": "He",
   "asr_first": "He",
   "word_start": 10.81,
   "onset": 10.81,
   "speech_end": 18.12,
   "start": 10.75,
   "end": 18.52,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 4,
   "text": "There, he shared a secret. The government planned to tear down the tower and sell its metal.",
   "first_word": "There,",
   "asr_first": "There,",
   "word_start": 18.58,
   "onset": 18.58,
   "speech_end": 23.14,
   "start": 18.52,
   "end": 23.54,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 5,
   "text": "One dealer, Andr\u00e9 Poisson, wanted the deal badly.",
   "first_word": "One",
   "asr_first": "One",
   "word_start": 23.6,
   "onset": 23.6,
   "speech_end": 26.52,
   "start": 23.54,
   "end": 26.95,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 6,
   "text": "But Lustig wanted more than the price of the tower.",
   "first_word": "But",
   "asr_first": "But",
   "word_start": 27.01,
   "onset": 27.01,
   "speech_end": 29.22,
   "start": 26.95,
   "end": 29.61,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 7,
   "text": "He hinted that he was a corrupt official. He expected a bribe, too.",
   "first_word": "He",
   "asr_first": "He",
   "word_start": 29.67,
   "onset": 29.67,
   "speech_end": 33.16,
   "start": 29.61,
   "end": 33.56,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 8,
   "text": "Strangely, that made the scam more convincing. Now there was a reason the deal happened behind closed doors.",
   "first_word": "Strangely,",
   "asr_first": "Strangely,",
   "word_start": 33.62,
   "onset": 33.62,
   "speech_end": 39.28,
   "start": 33.56,
   "end": 39.68,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 9,
   "text": "Poisson paid. Lustig took the money and fled to Austria.",
   "first_word": "Poisson",
   "asr_first": "Poisson",
   "word_start": 39.74,
   "onset": 39.74,
   "speech_end": 42.66,
   "start": 39.68,
   "end": 43.13,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 10,
   "text": "When Poisson realized he had been fooled, he was too embarrassed to go to the police.",
   "first_word": "When",
   "asr_first": "When",
   "word_start": 43.19,
   "onset": 43.19,
   "speech_end": 47.12,
   "start": 43.13,
   "end": 47.54,
   "speech_end_prev_ok": true
  },
  {
   "sentence": 11,
   "text": "The Eiffel Tower stayed right where it was. Poisson's money did not.",
   "first_word": "The",
   "asr_first": "The",
   "word_start": 47.6,
   "onset": 47.6,
   "speech_end": 51.26,
